# Sample entries appended to /etc/ettercap/etter.dns for the DNS Spoofing
# scenario (Chapter 5). Only the target domain (and its www subdomain) is
# redirected to the attacker's IP, so the victim's other DNS resolutions
# continue to work normally -- keeping the attack covert.
#
# Lab-only values: 192.168.0.133 is the Kali attacker VM on the isolated
# VMnet1 host-only segment (192.168.0.0/24). portal.corp-intranet.com is a
# fictitious internal hostname created for this lab, not a real domain.

mail.local A 192.168.0.133
www.portal.corp-intranet.com A 192.168.0.133
portal.corp-intranet.com A 192.168.0.133
